# 58. The One-Line Explanation of Each Major Layer

### Frontend

> React is responsible for the user interface, editors, navigation, state, and communicating with the backend.

### Backend

> Express is responsible for APIs, authentication, authorization, business logic, external integrations, exports, and WebSocket communication.

### Database/Data

> PlotForge currently uses a hybrid in-memory and file-backed JSON persistence layer, while the SQL schema is a future/relational reference.

### AI

> Gemini is accessed through a protected backend AI gateway that performs authentication, rate limiting, prompt construction, and streaming.

### WebSocket

> A custom lightweight STOMP-compatible WebSocket server provides authorized real-time collaboration between project members.

### Authentication

> JWT handles PlotForge sessions, bcrypt handles passwords, and Google/Firebase verifies external identities.

### TMDB

> TMDB supplies movie/series metadata while the backend keeps the API integration behind the server.

### Export

> PDFKit generates PDFs on the backend and the frontend downloads the generated binary.

### Testing

> Five test suites validate authentication, authorization, security, HTTP integration, and WebSocket behavior.

